Enhanced runtime and performance diagnostics: ao-vk
=================================================

The session-only Enhanced master hotkey (Ctrl+Shift+E), GPU cost display
(Ctrl+Shift+O) and slow-frame diagnostics follow ao-vk's user-facing features.
Sources inspected: proxy/ddraw/rvk_ddraw.cpp (master hotkey, profiling sweep,
50 ms slow-frame threshold), proxy/ddraw/rvk_settings.cpp (effective versus
stored settings), and rvk/profile.cpp (named GPU timestamps and deferred
query results), https://github.com/wannabuh/ao-vk at revision
47fceedf61d375947be20b78d97238cb9c971ca9.
The Rust/wgpu implementation is native and independent: it uses pass-boundary
timestamps, nonblocking readback and a live GUI-font overlay rather than
changing effects during a profiling sweep. No upstream artwork or binaries
are included. Copyright (c) 2026 wannabuh; the full MIT permission and warranty
notice reproduced above applies to these adaptations.

